course: dictionary
lesson: 11382
title: Formal words: abscond
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «The prisoner managed to abscond from the jail during the night.» Look at the clues: he escaped during the night, and nobody saw him go. To abscond means to leave secretly and suddenly, especially to escape or avoid being caught.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in: «The prisoner managed to run away secretly during the night» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Abscond is a formal word, so you will find it in news reports, police reports and serious stories.
explain: Abscond can also go with «with»: «The treasurer absconded with the club's money.» This means he ran away with money that was not his. Context tells you it was wrong, because he took something that belonged to other people.
fact: Abscond means to leave secretly and suddenly, especially to escape or avoid being caught.
fact: «Abscond with» means to run away with money or things that are not yours.
fact: Abscond is a formal verb: its forms are abscond, absconds, absconded and absconding.
fact: In everyday talk, children say «run off», and in the UK informal speech people say «do a runner».
fact: Clues in the sentence, such as «secretly», «suddenly» or «during the night», help you work out that abscond means sneaking away.
exercise: «The prisoner decided to abscond during the night.» What does abscond mean? | To make a loud noise | To eat a big breakfast | *To leave secretly and suddenly to escape | To sleep soundly in a bed
exercise: «The treasurer may abscond with the club funds.» What does abscond with mean here? | To count the money carefully | To give the money to a friend | To put the money in the bank | *To run away with money that is not his
exercise: Which everyday phrase means about the same as abscond? | Say hello | Have a long sleep | Build a sandcastle | *Do a runner
test: «The thief absconded before the police arrived.» Which words show that the thief left in secret and in a hurry? | *before the police arrived | He wore a red hat | The thief was tall | The sky was blue
test: What does abscond mean? | To paint a picture slowly | To arrive early for a party | *To leave secretly and suddenly, especially to escape | To check the time on a clock
exam: «The bank manager absconded with the money and was never seen again.» What does this tell us? | He gave the money to his best friend | He paid the money back the next day | He counted the money with the bank staff | *He ran away secretly with money that was not his
